License for the LibreCut community preset pack
=============================================

SPDX-License-Identifier: CC0-1.0
Canonical legal text: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode

What this covers
----------------

The preset *data* in this folder — the JSON manifest files and the numbers,
colour values, and names inside them — is dedicated to the public domain under
CC0 1.0 Universal.

To the extent possible under law, the contributors who authored these presets
have waived all copyright and related or neighbouring rights to them, and
dedicated them to the public domain worldwide. You may copy, modify, distribute,
and use these presets, including in commercial work, without attribution,
without permission, and without any obligation to share your own work under
the same terms.

The canonical CC0 1.0 text governs. The summary above is a convenience, not a
substitute for it.

What this does not cover
------------------------

The LibreCut application itself, its source code, and the documentation are
licensed separately under GPL-3.0-only. See the LICENSE file at the root of the
repository.

Installing a preset pack does not make the project you edit with it a
derivative work of LibreCut, and does not place any obligation on the video,
audio, or images you produce.

Third-party material
--------------------

A community preset pack must not contain third-party material. No LUT files,
fonts, textures, or brand assets may be included. Presets describe numbers and
colours that LibreCut's own inspector can reproduce; that is the whole
vocabulary of the format.

Contributions
-------------

By contributing a preset to this folder you agree that your contribution is
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal, matching the licence
above. See docs/community-presets.md for the review criteria and the
submission process.
